/E (  A Stanford University study showed that homework affects students' physical and mental health because at least 56% of students attribute homework as their primary source of stress. This tells us that many students find homework to be stressful, partly because of how some students rush through it the night before. To prevent such matters from occurring, one solution is to get your homework done as soon as possible. By doing so, you do not have to worry about it piling up, then rushing it at the last minute.  )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4 5]
>>
endobj
95 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (  On top of everything else, after school activities such as Co-Curriculum Activities \(CCAs\) as well as tuition prevent students from finishing their work on time. Because of all these after school activities, students will tend to come up with reasons such as not having enough time to do as well as being too tired to do any work. In order to prevent such things from happening, students can come forward and voice their opinions to the teachers to let them know that they are unable to balance their time management and work, requiring  more time.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6 7]
>>
endobj
96 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (  However, homework can help us in some ways. One is that we can use it to gauge whether we genuinely understood the lesson the teacher has gone through in class. It also helps the teacher understand which part of the lesson you have not understood and can be improved, thus helping us understand the concepts and topics better. Another way homework can help us is that it can boosts our knowledge on that particular chapter. By doing so, students can then improve and score better. Therefore, there are times when homework can be valuable and helpful to us. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8 9]
>>
endobj
