106 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 70 0 R
/E (Some people want the mandatory death sentence to end\(perhaps lighter sentencing depending on the offence\), while others want Singapore to completely abolish it. The U.N. Human Rights Office notes that Singapore's strict drug policies unfairly target underprivileged communities and do little to stop the flow of drugs into and out of the city-state. Punishing a single dealer/drug mule \(people hired to transport drugs\) does not change the fact that it barely fixes the problem; mules can be easily replaced and the people behind such twisted schemes simply earn and laugh in profit. Experts around the world agree there is no evidence proving death sentences are better at deterring crime than other punishments, such as life in prison. But so far, the Singapore government is standing firmly behind its use of the death penalty as a deterrent, ramping up the pace of executions even as other countries in the region relax their drug laws.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
