/P 72 0 R
/T (So, how did Roe v. Wade come about in the first place? In 1969, American activist Norma McCorvey, who went by the pseudonym, Jane Roe, attempted to get an abortion in Texas. Howbeit, she was not given a chance to do so. This was owing to the fact that there were no abortion clinics at all in Texas. Abortion was illegal in Texas \(except when to save someone's life\). Her two attorneys filed a lawsuit pertaining to the matter against US District Attorney Henry Wade, who argued that the abortion laws were in accordance with the US Constitution.)
/E (So, how did Roe v. Wade come about in the first place? In 1969, American activist Norma McCorvey, who went by the pseudonym, Jane Roe, attempted to get an abortion in Texas. Howbeit, she was not given a chance to do so. This was owing to the fact that there were no abortion clinics at all in Texas. Abortion was illegal in Texas \(except when to save someone's life\). Her two attorneys filed a lawsuit pertaining to the matter against US District Attorney Henry Wade, who argued that the abortion laws were in accordance with the US Constitution.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
