/E (The price of housing in Singapore is influenced by the state of the economy and the population growth, and due to the large population for the small land surface area in Singapore, the housing prices are slowly increasing. The prices of private homes have risen 18.6% since 2020 at the onset of Covid. A partial reason for the increasing prices is due to more foreigners buying properties in Singapore, because regardless of their residential status in Singapore, they will still enjoy less strict restrictions surrounding the purchase of private housing. Another reason is that there is a disruption in the supply chain which started to emerge in late 2020, and it is causing delays in new projects, and hence more people are turning to pre-owned properties. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
